  "content": {
    "id": "p24-q6-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "6",
    "prompt": "Solve these non-linear equations simultaneously by substitution.\nThere are two possible sets of solutions.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 3,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p24-q6-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$$\\begin{aligned}x+y&=15\\quad(1)\\\\x^2+y^2&=125\\quad(2)\\end{aligned}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(5,10)$ and $(10,5)$",
          "worked": "Rearrange (1): $y=15-x$. Substitute into (2).\n$$\\begin{align*}x^2+(15-x)^2&=125\\\\x^2+225-30x+x^2&=125\\\\2x^2-30x+100&=0\\\\x^2-15x+50&=0\\\\(x-5)(x-10)&=0\\\\x&=5\\text{ or }10\\end{align*}$$\nSubstitute back into $y=15-x$.\n$$\\begin{align*}x=5:\\quad y&=15-5=10\\\\x=10:\\quad y&=15-10=5\\end{align*}$$\nSolutions: $(5,10)$ and $(10,5)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 95
      },
      {
        "id": "p24-q6-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$$\\begin{aligned}x-y&=3\\quad(1)\\\\x^2+y^2&=185\\quad(2)\\end{aligned}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(-8,-11)$ and $(11,8)$",
          "worked": "Rearrange (1): $y=x-3$. Substitute into (2).\n$$\\begin{align*}x^2+(x-3)^2&=185\\\\x^2+x^2-6x+9&=185\\\\2x^2-6x-176&=0\\\\x^2-3x-88&=0\\\\(x-11)(x+8)&=0\\\\x&=11\\text{ or }-8\\end{align*}$$\nSubstitute back into $y=x-3$.\n$$\\begin{align*}x=-8:\\quad y&=-8-3=-11\\\\x=11:\\quad y&=11-3=8\\end{align*}$$\nSolutions: $(-8,-11)$ and $(11,8)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 95
      },
      {
        "id": "p24-q6-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$$\\begin{aligned}2x+y&=5\\quad(1)\\\\4x^2+y^2&=17\\quad(2)\\end{aligned}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\left(\\frac12,4\\right)$ and $(2,1)$",
          "worked": "Rearrange (1): $y=5-2x$. Substitute into (2).\n$$\\begin{align*}4x^2+(5-2x)^2&=17\\\\4x^2+25-20x+4x^2&=17\\\\8x^2-20x+8&=0\\\\2x^2-5x+2&=0\\\\(2x-1)(x-2)&=0\\\\x&=\\frac12\\text{ or }2\\end{align*}$$\nSubstitute back into $y=5-2x$.\n$$\\begin{align*}x=\\frac12:\\quad y&=5-2\\left(\\frac12\\right)=4\\\\x=2:\\quad y&=5-2(2)=1\\end{align*}$$\nSolutions: $\\left(\\frac12,4\\right)$ and $(2,1)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 100
      },
      {
        "id": "p24-q6-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$$\\begin{aligned}x+y&=9\\quad(1)\\\\x^2+xy+y^2&=61\\quad(2)\\end{aligned}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(4,5)$ and $(5,4)$",
          "worked": "Rearrange (1): $y=9-x$. Substitute into (2).\n$$\\begin{align*}x^2+x(9-x)+(9-x)^2&=61\\\\x^2+9x-x^2+81-18x+x^2&=61\\\\x^2-9x+20&=0\\\\(x-4)(x-5)&=0\\\\x&=4\\text{ or }5\\end{align*}$$\nSubstitute back into $y=9-x$.\n$$\\begin{align*}x=4:\\quad y&=9-4=5\\\\x=5:\\quad y&=9-5=4\\end{align*}$$\nSolutions: $(4,5)$ and $(5,4)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 100
      },
      {
        "id": "p24-q6-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$$\\begin{aligned}x+2y&=5\\quad(1)\\\\2xy-x^2&=3\\quad(2)\\end{aligned}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(1,2)$ and $\\left(\\frac32,\\frac74\\right)$",
          "worked": "Rearrange (1): $x=5-2y$. Substitute into (2).\n$$\\begin{align*}2(5-2y)y-(5-2y)^2&=3\\\\10y-4y^2-25+20y-4y^2&=3\\\\8y^2-30y+28&=0\\\\4y^2-15y+14&=0\\\\(4y-7)(y-2)&=0\\\\y&=\\frac74\\text{ or }2\\end{align*}$$\nSubstitute back into $x=5-2y$.\n$$\\begin{align*}y=2:\\quad x&=5-2(2)=1\\\\y=\\frac74:\\quad x&=5-2\\left(\\frac74\\right)=\\frac32\\end{align*}$$\nSolutions: $(1,2)$ and $\\left(\\frac32,\\frac74\\right)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 110
      },
      {
        "id": "p24-q6-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$$\\begin{aligned}3x+2y&=16\\quad(1)\\\\xy&=10\\quad(2)\\end{aligned}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(2,5)$ and $\\left(\\frac{10}{3},3\\right)$",
          "worked": "Rearrange (1): $y=\\frac{16-3x}{2}$. Substitute into (2).\n$$\\begin{align*}x\\left(\\frac{16-3x}{2}\\right)&=10\\\\16x-3x^2&=20\\\\3x^2-16x+20&=0\\\\(3x-10)(x-2)&=0\\\\x&=\\frac{10}{3}\\text{ or }2\\end{align*}$$\nSubstitute back into $y=\\frac{16-3x}{2}$.\n$$\\begin{align*}x=2:\\quad y&=\\frac{16-3(2)}{2}=5\\\\x=\\frac{10}{3}:\\quad y&=\\frac{16-3\\left(\\frac{10}{3}\\right)}{2}=3\\end{align*}$$\nSolutions: $(2,5)$ and $\\left(\\frac{10}{3},3\\right)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 105
      }
    ]
  },
